       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A single 2,550 mg dose, repeated three times a day for 7,650 mg/day, is about 3 times the maximum labeled daily dose. It could cause severe lactic acidosis, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. I don't know of any indication that would justify it, and I can't undo the order once it reaches the patient.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, or another regimen at or below 2,550 mg/day.\n\nIf you have a specific reason for a higher dose, such as a protocol or a research setting, that decision should go through pharmacy review and your institution's high-dose override process, not through me.\n\nWhich of the options above would you like me to enter?"
